{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510970-awakened-demographics","id":1510970,"title":"Awakened demographics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-07T03:46:38-07:00","id":1510970,"title":"Awakened demographics","content":"Does anyone have numbers? Ideally, with a source if possible<br /> I recall order of Hermes second edition saying &quot;one in 5 million&quot;, <br /> TOJ says 3000 traditionalists and 5000 technocrats albeit only in the context of a specific battle.<br /> Even books which say &quot;hundreds&quot; or &quot;thousands&quot; are welcome, so long as you are certain that they differentiate the Awakened from, say , extraordinary citizens<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, do any books say which Traditions?conventions are smaller/bigger? For instance, order of hermes second edition, says, even OOC that they are probably the largest one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T04:17:41-07:00","id":1510971,"title":"","content":"I always go back to the WoD Population Project for such questions: <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20201112011225/http://shadownessence.org/index.php?/topic/20000-owod-population-project/\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20201112...ation-project/</a><br /> <br /> Which states: &quot;There are two conflicting accounts. 1 in a million in a few older sources, and 1 in 150,000 mortals in Fallen Tower: Las Vegas. The first number doesn't leave enough mages for all their societies. The second, newer number incorporates all the sorcerers as well, which outnumber mages 3 to 1.&quot; So that would be 1 fully Awakened for every 600,000 Sleepers.<br /> <br /> My head-canon for why there's two conflicting accounts is that there's a pre-Avatar Storm number and a post-Avatar Storm one. In the latter case there's more mages on physical Earth cause they're mostly stuck here. Before then Awakened had a tendency of wandering off into the Umbra or to Horizon Realms. So there was a higher turnover rate before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2198,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","user":"Malkavian87","date":". 05-07-2023, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T04:45:41-07:00","id":1510974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510970-awakened-demographics?p=1510971#post1510971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always go back to the WoD Population Project for such questions: <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20201112011225/http://shadownessence.org/index.php?/topic/20000-owod-population-project/\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20201112...ation-project/</a><br /> <br /> Which states: &quot;There are two conflicting accounts. 1 in a million in a few older sources, and 1 in 150,000 mortals in Fallen Tower: Las Vegas. The first number doesn't leave enough mages for all their societies. The second, newer number incorporates all the sorcerers as well, which outnumber mages 3 to 1.&quot; So that would be 1 fully Awakened for every 600,000 Sleepers.<br /> <br /> My head-canon for why there's two conflicting accounts is that there's a pre-Avatar Storm number and a post-Avatar Storm one. In the latter case there's more mages on physical Earth cause they're mostly stuck here. Before then Awakened had a tendency of wandering off into the Umbra or to Horizon Realms. So there was a higher turnover rate before.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem is that there are a lot more sorcerers than 3 to 1 at least according to other sources such as books of crafts, though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T05:37:18-07:00","id":1510976,"title":"","content":"Let me point you to <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/299324\" target=\"_blank\"> Ascension's Landscape</a>, one of the better researched and written Storyteller's Vault products, which tackles this and other questions in detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T12:20:49-07:00","id":1511009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510970-awakened-demographics?p=1510974#post1510974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only problem is that there are a lot more sorcerers than 3 to 1 at least according to other sources such as books of crafts, though</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a weird statement considering that Book of Crafts predates the Sorceror book and doesn't imply that any of the Crafts are actually staffed by Sorcerors as we would term them today.There is a clear reference to the spheres that are being thought, there are rotes, and the few unawakened with powers in the book are the ones that let an external thing into them to empower them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T20:44:53-07:00","id":1511042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510970-awakened-demographics?p=1511009#post1511009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a weird statement considering that Book of Crafts predates the Sorceror book and doesn't imply that any of the Crafts are actually staffed by Sorcerors as we would term them today.There is a clear reference to the spheres that are being thought, there are rotes, and the few unawakened with powers in the book are the ones that let an external thing into them to empower them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What i meant is that it explicitly gives demographics. Such as the bata'a. I can not remember the actual numbers per craft, but it was a lot. Sorcerers existed since before even &quot;world of darkness sorcerer. &quot;<br /> <br /> At any rate, i do not care that much about sorcerers. Any chance you know other sources? I seem to recall that DA: mage said something about the subject but i can not recall (this is extremely important for me, because i plan to make a 12 century chronicle so..)<br /> Of course, the demographics back then had a lot more mages than today due to magic not being &quot;dead&quot;, but whatever<br /> Having said that, does Las vegas by night explicitly state that sorcerers are 3 times more than mages&gt; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2198_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2198\" data-vbnamecard=\"2198\">Malkavian87</a> ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T04:02:31-07:00","id":1511063,"title":"","content":"You're correct in that the Book of Crafts gives numbers for most of them, though it doesn't clearly delineate betwee &quot;just&quot; an acolyte and a hedge magician in quite a few of the entries, at times even conflating them together. I seem to have glossed over that beyond them being small.<br /> <br /> However, why is this important to you? The WoD in general works with &quot;the population density is exactly what the plot needs it to be&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T14:15:31-07:00","id":1511083,"title":"","content":"I get wondering about a canon number, as to give your setting some internal consistency. As an ST you then still have free reign to come up with an exception to the rule for the area where your chronicle is set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T02:24:02-07:00","id":1511113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1510970-awakened-demographics?p=1511063#post1511063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're correct in that the Book of Crafts gives numbers for most of them, though it doesn't clearly delineate betwee &quot;just&quot; an acolyte and a hedge magician in quite a few of the entries, at times even conflating them together. I seem to have glossed over that beyond them being small.<br /> <br /> However, why is this important to you? The WoD in general works with &quot;the population density is exactly what the plot needs it to be&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple curiosity.<br /> Also I need to somehow justify the absolutely insane situation of the conversion of house tremere and how nobody found out for 180 years. Anyway this a discussion for a future thread on the vampire forums.<br /> <br /> Tradition Book order of hermes second edition gave the 1 in 5 million numbers but I am curious as to what Phil brucatto had on mind. It's a bit too low right?<br /> <br /> Edit. Just wanted to clarify that I am not blaming the writer in any sense, I am genuinely curious as to why demographics were that low in some books","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 05-09-2023, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}